 "notes": [
  "DateInput is a custom input: name it `form.<key>` and read it as `form.<key>` (here `form.dateOfBirth`).",
  "It posts a number, epoch milliseconds, not a `YYYY-MM-DD` string. With `utc-time: true` the number is UTC midnight of the chosen day, so the date is the same in every time zone; without it, it is local midnight in the user's browser and can read as the day before in UTC.",
  "In a scriptlet: `const dob = new Date(Number(value));` then use `dob.getUTCFullYear()`, `dob.getUTCMonth()` (0-11) and `dob.getUTCDate()`; an age check compares those with today's UTC date. Check for an empty value (`\"\"`) first.",
  "`format` (`MM/DD/YYYY`) only changes how the date is shown and typed; `years-range` limits the years the calendar offers.",
  "Ids are console-shaped: screenId \"SC\" + 27 base62 chars, node ids 10-char nanoids equal to props.id. Using this screen twice in one flow: give the copy a new screenId (node ids only need to be unique within a screen)."
 ]
}
